(EXP-60: `3.14 as a number` truncates to 3.
 Also covers: EXP-61 `42 as a float`, EXP-62 `25 as text`, EXP-63
 `"123" as a number`, EXP-64 `3.14 as text`, EXP-65 `"3.14" as a float`,
 EXP-66 `true as a number`, EXP-67 `false as a number`, EXP-68
 `0 as a boolean`, EXP-69 `42 as a boolean`, EXP-70 `true as text`, EXP-71
 `"true" as a boolean` - every row of the Basic Conversions table except the
 buffer one, which is EXP-72.
 EXP-68 and EXP-71 are recorded through `as text` rather than bare: booleans
 print as 1/0 per LANGUAGE.md:2238, so a bare Print cannot tell the manual's
 documented `false` result from a number 0. Rendering the boolean back to text
 shows the cast really produced a boolean, and the `'s type` line confirms it.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-60.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   3
   42.0
   25
   123
   3.14
   3.14
   1
   0
   false
   true
   true
   true
   Boolean (static)
)
Print 3.14 as a number.
Print 42 as a float.
Print 25 as text.
Print "123" as a number.
Print 3.14 as text.
Print "3.14" as a float.
